    "title": "SPF Sunscreen: Understanding Protection Levels and Choosing the Right Number",
    "question": "What SPF sunscreen do I actually need, and does a higher number meaningfully protect me more?",
    "summary": "SPF measures a sunscreen's ability to block UVB rays, but protection does not scale linearly — SPF 30 blocks ~97% of UVB rays while SPF 50 blocks ~98%, making reapplication and broad-spectrum coverage equally important considerations as the SPF number itself.",
